---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-2">CRUD HTML | JS | PHP</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-16">
    <h1 class="font-bold text-2xl">CONNECTION</h1>
    <p>
      To connect to a MySQL database called <code>dbhospital</code> hosted on
      <code>localhost</code> using the username <code>root</code> and no password.
      If the connection fails, it displays an error message.
    </p>


    <div class="bg-[#23272e] text-[#f8f8f2] p-4 rounded-md mt-4">
     <pre><code class="language-php">
&lt;?php
    $servername = "localhost";
    $dbusername = "root";
    $dbpassword = "";
    $dbname = "database_name";

    try &#123;
        $conn = new PDO("mysql:host=$servername;dbname=$dbname", $dbusername, $dbpassword);
        $conn->setAttribute(PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE, PDO::ERRMODE_EXCEPTION);

    &#125; catch(PDOException $e) &#123;
        echo "Connection failed: " . $e->getMessage();
        die;  
    &#125;
?&gt;
    </code></pre>
    </div>

<div class="mt-16">
    <h1 align="center" class="font-bold text-2xl">PHP Backend Code</h1>
    <p>
     The purpose of your PHP code is to act as a simple back-end API that allows you to create, read, update, and delete (CRUD) user records in a database via HTTP requests, using Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) for better structure and reusability.
    </p>
 <h1 class="font-bold text-2xl border-b-4 w-fit  pr-3 mt-3">Class</h1>
    <p>
     a class is a blueprint for creating objects. It helps organize code and group related functionality together. The main purpose of using a class is to implement Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), which improves modularity, reusability, and maintainability.
    </p>
<div class="bg-[#23272e] text-[#f8f8f2] p-4 rounded-md mt-4">
     <pre><code class="language-php">
&lt;?php
class User  &#123
    function save($json)(
      //put here the save function logic
    );
    function getRecords(
      //put here the getRecords function logic
    );
    function update($json)(
      //put here the update function logic
    );
    function delete($json)(
      //put here the delete function logic
    );
 &#125
?&gt;
    </code></pre>
    </div>
</div>


<div class="mt-16">
    <h1 class="font-bold text-2xl border-b-4 w-fit  pr-3 mt-3">Function save</h1>
    <p>
      it can be use to save data to the database. It should be able to handle the data sent from the frontend and save it to database.
    </p>
    

<div class="bg-[#23272e] text-[#f8f8f2] p-4 rounded-md mt-4">
     <pre><code class="language-php">
&lt;?php
class User  &#123
    function save($json)(
      include "connection.php";
        $json = json_decode($json, true);

        $fname = $json['fname'];
        $mname = $json['mname'];
        $lname = $json['lname'];

        $sql = "INSERT INTO user (fname, mname, lname) VALUES (:firstName, :middlename,
         :lastName)";
        $stmt = $conn->prepare($sql);
        $stmt->bindParam(":firstName", $fname);
        $stmt->bindParam(":middlename", $mname);
        $stmt->bindParam(":lastName", $lname);

        $stmt->execute();
        $returnValue = $stmt->rowCount() > 0 ? 1 : 0;

        return $returnValue;
    );
    
 &#125
?&gt;
    </code></pre>
    </div>
</div>

</BaseLayout>